WEBVTT

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.850
If you put your dog in a big wooden box with a door in the middle, it already has a home.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.830
But on the first cold night, it curls up as tight as it can and shivers.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:12.440
Its own body is the only heater in there.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.990
And you gave it a room far too big to warm, so you make it smaller, just big enough to stand up,

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.240
turn around and lie down, that's the fit, but the box sits right on the ground,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.920
it rains and the damp creeps up through the floor.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.630
So you lift it onto bricks and the floor stays dry, that's the raised floor, but the floor is hard,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.530
so you give it your softest blanket.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.680
And your dog walks in soaking wet.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.470
The blanket drinks it all up.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.250
And on a freezing night, a wet blanket freezes,

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.920
so you take it out and fill the bed with straw Dr straw keeps out the cold and the damp, that's the straw,

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:50.110
but every time your dog walks out the straw goes with it, so you raise the bottom of the doorway.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:55.760
About five inches the straw stays in and now it has somewhere to rest its chin, that's the sill,

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.780
but the walls are thin and the warmth leaks away so you line the walls,

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.130
the floor and the ceiling with foam and cover it with wood.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.800
That's the insulation. Now it really has everything until the wind picks up.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:14.040
Do is in the middle, so the wind blows straight in right onto the bed. you hang a flap over the door, it helps.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:20.700
Bed is still right behind it because look inside a doghouse designed by an animal charity, it isn't one room,

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.470
it's two the door goes at one end and it opens into a little hallway your dog walks in,

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.770
turns the corner and sleeps behind a wall.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.930
For a retriever, the bedroom is only 22 inches by 39.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:40.960
Now the wind hits the wall, not your dog, that's the side door in summer you take the flap off and move the whole house into the shade so if your dog's door is in the middle,

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.810
Turn it away from the wind.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.280
Hang a flap and swap the blanket for straw.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.450
And on the coldest nights, the best dog house is yours.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.310
And that's how.
